upgrade upg:cue-schemas-installed
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  location ~/Documents/Bonfyre/schemas/bonfyre.cue plus vet.sh
  claim Bonfyre state is now schema-enforced rather than convention-enforced.
  covers PartnerProfile, PartnerProfileStrict, FundingRoute, PriceEvidence, EconomicMeasure, SolvedInvariant, Capability
  passes 176 profiles, 3 funding routes, 19 invariants, 15 capabilities
  gate vet.sh exits nonzero on violation, so it is usable as a gate and not merely a report

claim clm:cue-has-teeth
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim The schemas reject bad state, proven by negative test rather than assumed.
  rejected a capability at maturity 'promoted' carrying proof_ref 'pending'
  rejected a SolvedInvariant with an empty reheat_conditions list
  encoded an EconomicMeasure at basis 'unknown' must carry unknown_reason and must NOT carry an amount; at any other basis it must carry currency and amount. That forbids both failure modes seen this session -- guessing a number into the ledger, and omitting the reason from an unknown.
  encoded PriceEvidence must be bitemporal; effective_at and observed_at are different facts and financial_metabolism rejects a price carrying only one
  encoded every partner must declare a non-ownership boundary; all 176 pass the strict schema

claim clm:cue-caught-my-own-inconsistency
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  finding 15 program capabilities used uppercase public_names (bonfyre.program.A-opportunity-fabric) against an estate convention of lowercase
  resolution the DATA was normalised, not the schema loosened
  note this is the value of a schema over a convention: the convention had been violated by me, silently, fifteen times

