# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# METHODS THAT COULD NOT BE EXECUTED, AND WHY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim clm:bonfyre-canon-grammar-is-json-only
  status STANDING
  verification REPRODUCED
  claim bonfyre-canon advertises Tree-sitter structural canonicalization but supports only .json
  evidence status returns ok; hash on a .py file returns 'Unsupported file type'; the binary's embedded extension table contains .json alone
  consequence it cannot perform structural duplicate detection over the control plane, which is Python; that is why the duplicate-mechanic census was done by reading rather than by structural hashing
  action_required a Python grammar would make Program O's census mechanical rather than manual

claim clm:most-partner-methods-are-not-installed
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim The commons lists 176 methods; the machine can execute a small fraction of them.
  present cue, duckdb, zstd, wasmtime, helm, kubectl, docker, ffmpeg, llama-cli, bonfyre-canon, bonfyre-pack, and the bonfyre-* native family
  absent tigerbeetle, formance, feldera, restate, lance, iroh, nix, terraform, pulumi, tree-sitter CLI, simdjson, mlflow, dvc, and every Python quant library (vectorbt, qlib, riskfolio, QuantLib, nautilus_trader, arcticdb, deepeval)
  consequence a profile at maturity 'defined' whose binary is absent cannot be promoted past 'defined' honestly; the capability ladder's rung 3 (installed) is the real gate and most of the commons has not passed it
  note llama-cli is present but the only local model in cache is nomic-embed-text, an embedding model, so local GENERATION is unavailable without a further download; the zero-token inference path is therefore still unproven

